        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="can run">can run</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="cans run">cans run</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="can runs">can runs</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Can I" data-hint="You are asking permission for your own action, so begin Can I." data-fix="Can I use your phone for a minute?">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. ___ use your phone for a minute? My battery is dead.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Can I">Can I</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I can">I can</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do I can">Do I can</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="can’t" data-hint="The confirmed work shift makes coming unavailable tonight, so use can’t." data-fix="Sorry, we can’t come tonight because we are working.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. A confirmed work shift makes the visit impossible: Sorry, we ___ come tonight because we are working.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="can’t">can’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="don’t can">don’t can</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="aren’t can">aren’t can</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="can’t" data-hint="The prompt requests one word, so keep can and contract not without repeating cook." data-fix="Can your fictional brother cook? No, he can’t.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. Complete the short answer with one word: “Can your fictional brother cook?” “No, he ___.”</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="can’t">can’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="doesn’t">doesn’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="can’t cook">can’t cook</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="speak" data-hint="A modal is followed directly by the base verb, with no -s and no to." data-fix="The profile says she can speak Spanish and Portuguese.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. Complete the fictional language profile: She can ___ Spanish and Portuguese.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="speak">speak</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="speaks">speaks</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="to speak">to speak</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Can she drive?" data-hint="Move Can before she and keep drive in its base form; do not add does." data-fix="The correct ability question is: Can she drive?">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. Which question correctly asks about the fictional traveler’s driving ability?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Can she drive?">Can she drive?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Does she can drive?">Does she can drive?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Can she drives?">Can she drives?</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="permission" data-hint="A manager is allowing an employee’s action, not describing a skill." data-fix="When a manager says, 'You can leave early today,' can gives permission.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. A manager says, “You can leave early today.” Which meaning is this?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="permission">permission</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="ability">ability</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a request">a request</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a request" data-hint="The speaker wants the listener to perform the helpful action." data-fix="Can you help me with these bags? is a request for action.">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. A traveler points to two heavy bags and asks, “Can you help me with these bags?” Which meaning is this?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a request">a request</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an ability question">an ability question</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a permission question">a permission question</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check quiz</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset quiz</button>
